  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nThe weather pattern favors temperatures to remain at or above\nnormal through the remainder of the weekend and into late next\nweek. In addition, dry weather is expected as the subtropical\nridge remains the dominant weather feature through the forecast\nperiod. Some of the medium range models do show a weak, mid-level\nshear axis dropping southward out of north Texas late Saturday\ninto Sunday. We will monitor this and see if any convection that\ndevelops to our north sends any outflow boundaries southward. At\nthis time, confidence is too low to mention any rain chances for\nour northern areas (Hill Country and I-35 corridor north of\nAustin). Also, we can't rule out some isolated convection over the\ncoastal plains region and may need to add some low chances for\nthis early next week. \n\nTemperatures appear to slowly inch upward, especially as we head\ninto the middle of next week. We could see some heat index values\nnudge upward toward the 108 degree mark for areas along and east\nof I-35 possibly beginning as early as Tuesday. Both the ECMWF and\nGFS MOS guidance agree in showing highs trending above normal for\nmuch of the mid to late portion of next week as mid and upper\nlevel high pressure over the Gulf builds into south Texas.",
